From 0095f01f40defaa9266e5f24af3baa141344093a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shuxueshuxue <shuxue@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:34:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] gugu: offer Claude's UltraCode as a session effort

Why: UltraCode (xhigh effort plus standing dynamic-workflow orchestration) is
a session flag in Claude Code (`ultracode` in flag settings), not an
EffortLevel, so ACP clients have no way to pick it. Gugu offers it as one more
row of the effort picker on models that support `xhigh`: picking it applies
`{ultracode: true, effortLevel: null}`; leaving it applies the new effort and
`ultracode: false` in the same update; a model switch to a model without
`xhigh` clears it. Sessions that never touch UltraCode keep the plain
`effortLevel` update, so other clients see no change.

Upstream: to be proposed as a general capability (expose Claude's ultracode
switch to ACP clients); no upstream PR yet.

Drop when: upstream exposes UltraCode through configOptions (or an
extension point Gugu can use without patching).
